# --- guards against the 2026-09-17 incident (brain backlog B11) -------------
#
# The rules above ignore generated output by PATH (`results/`, `resources/`,
# `data/`). Git ignore rules are path-based, so RENAMING those directories
# moves 662 MB of regenerable output out from under them. That is exactly what
# happened: a cleanup renamed them into `.trash-20260901/` -- because the
# cluster's policy denies `rm -rf` -- a `git add -A` swept them in, and the
# 177.67 MB parquet inside blocked every push to GitHub for two weeks until
# the history had to be rewritten.
#
# So: ignore the SHAPE of the thing as well as its location. Delete
# regenerable folders with `rm -r` (which IS permitted); never rename them
# aside.
.trash*/
*.orig
*.rej

# Slurm job logs land in the repo root and were neither ignored nor committed
# -- one careless `git add -A` from repeating the incident.
slurm-*.out
slurm-*.err

# Bulk scientific data formats. Legitimate inputs live under
# workflow/repo_data/ and workflow/geodata_repo/, which are re-included below;
# anywhere else these are pipeline output and must not enter git.
*.nc
*.pkl
*.parquet
*.gpkg
*.tif
*.tiff
!workflow/repo_data/**
!workflow/geodata_repo/**
!natura.tiff

